        "id": 1002885
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-20T10:18:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`call_noreply()` blocks pldmd until the processor replies(with ~25s default timeout).\nSince the result is only logged, shall we make it `call_async()` instead?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 684,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 684,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "49d66e662c3c4f63957d8767194335b4078a1428",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b0b7d4af_e3640cf9",
        "filename": "platform-mc/event_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 684,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000086
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T06:08:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The use case here is mainly to hand off the CPER payload for processing and return. Do you happen to have any measurements or traces showing that call_noreply() is blocking in this path? It would also be helpful to understand any fd ownership/lifetime considerations before switching to call_async().",
      "parentUuid": "8150a460_f22dcb7b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 684,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 684,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "49d66e662c3c4f63957d8767194335b4078a1428",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c9e4a2a4_a714a155",
        "filename": "platform-mc/event_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 684,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002885
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T09:55:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No measurements, but I follows the code in the following link:\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/sdbusplus/blob/c6176961f4a2db9a78653b990db0fad4aaecf325/include/sdbusplus/bus.hpp#L366\n\n`sd_bus_call()` polls until the matching reply or the 25s default timeout. Just thinking if this would become a blocker under some critical situation.",
      "parentUuid": "b0b7d4af_e3640cf9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 684,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 684,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "49d66e662c3c4f63957d8767194335b4078a1428",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "39918f86_07f9d9cc",
        "filename": "platform-mc/event_manager.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 684,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000086
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T11:11:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that call_noreply() is synchronous. Do we have any data showing this is a real issue in practice? The CPER processor daemon already takes ownership of the payload and handles processing. I\u0027d prefer to avoid additional async complexity without evidence of a bottleneck. Reference: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/q/topic:%22cper-processor-daemon%22",
      "parentUuid": "c9e4a2a4_a714a155",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 684,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 684,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "49d66e662c3c4f63957d8767194335b4078a1428",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
